.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt VFS_MOUNT 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm vfs_mount
.Nd mount a filesystem
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In vfs/vfs.h
.Ft int
.Fn vfs_mount "const char *device" "const char *path" "const char *type" "uint32_t flags" "void *data"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vfs_mount
function mounts a filesystem of the specified
.Fa type
onto the directory specified by
.Fa path .
.Pp
The
.Fa device
argument specifies the source device (e.g., "/dev/hda") or a special identifier depending on the filesystem type.
.Pp
The
.Fa flags
and
.Fa data
arguments provide generic and filesystem-specific mount options, respectively.
.Pp
If
.Fa path
is "/", the filesystem is mounted as the root filesystem
.Pq Va fs_root .
Otherwise, the function looks up the mount point node and attaches the new filesystem root to it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn vfs_mount
function returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfs 9 ,
.Xr vfs_lookup 9 ,
.Xr vfs_register_filesystem 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn vfs_mount
function appeared in Substrate.
